window.docContents[9].resolve({"/Tate-algebras-and-the-structure-sheaf/#Adic-Spaces-___-Lean-blueprint--Tate-algebras-and-the-structure-sheaf":{"contents":"The Tate algebra  over a Tate ring \n() is the ring of restricted power series — those whose\ncoefficients tend to  — the building block of the structure sheaf on rational\nsubsets of . In Adic-Spaces this is\n. Following Wedhorn Definition 7.29.\n\n(Tate's acyclicity theorem / the structure sheaf.) For a strongly noetherian\nTate ring, the structure presheaf  on the rational subsets of\n (, )\nis a sheaf: the Čech complex of a rational cover is exact (Tate acyclicity),\nso sections glue. This makes  an\nadic space.\nIn Adic-Spaces:  (Adic spaces/StructureSheaf.lean)\n— in progress (the Laurent-cover acyclicity and the gluing refinement carry the\nremaining sorrys).\n\n","context":"Adic Spaces — Lean blueprint","header":"4. Tate algebras and the structure sheaf","id":"/Tate-algebras-and-the-structure-sheaf/#Adic-Spaces-___-Lean-blueprint--Tate-algebras-and-the-structure-sheaf"}});